From: Hummingbird <hummingbird@redhat.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Bump klauspost/compress to v1.20.2 and OpenTelemetry-Go to v1.47.0

Keep in sync with go-vendor-tools.toml's matching pre_commands. The updated
vendor tarball (Source1) carries the matching vendor tree and
vendor/modules.txt; this patch updates only go.mod and go.sum.

CVE-2026-116591: crafted zstd input panics DecodeAll and the streaming
decoder via a bad normalized FSE count (klauspost/compress v1.20.2).

CVE-2026-128085: OpenTelemetry-Go attribute truncation bypass. otel, sdk,
trace, metric, sdk/metric, log and sdk/log are bumped to v1.47.0, the OTLP and
stdout exporters to v1.47.0 (v0.23.0 for the log exporters), and
google.golang.org/genproto/googleapis/{api,rpc} follow as required by them.

